    "title": "Raelene Ann Wharton, 96, Remembered for Love of Golf and Gardening",
    "text": "Raelene A. Wharton | Anderson Memorial Home & Heartland Cremation Services\nRaelene A. Wharton | Anderson Memorial Home & Heartland Cremation Services\nShe is survived by her loving children Rae Hibner, Doug Lyons, Nancy Horn, Linda Lyons, and Suzanne (Rob) Tauler; brother Quentin (Shirley) Warren; grandchildren Kevin Hibner, Thomas Hibner, Christina Lyons, Kristen (Caleb) Stine, Nicole (Jason) Rautbort, Alexis (Craig) Long, Sean Tauler, Gillian Tauler, and Ethan Tauler; great-grandchildren Elijah, Kayshawn, Kaden, Kiara, Ka’miyah, Summer, Skylee, Scarlette, Dorianne, Abigail, Byerlee, and Camden, along with numerous nieces and nephews.\nPreceding her in death were her parents Gilbert and Amy Warren, her first husband Richard D. Lyons, late husband M. Ben Wharton, and great-grandson Nathan.\nVisitation will be held on Monday from 3:00 pm to 7:00 pm, with a celebration of her life to begin at 6:00 pm at Anderson Memorial Home in Plainfield, IL. Family and friends are invited to meet at North Shore Garden of Memories in North Chicago on Tuesday at 11:00 am for interment and committal prayers, without procession.\nClick here to read the original obituary.",
